			"date": "2023-05-03T15:19:19.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://hachyderm.io/@andydavies\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>andydavies</span></a></span> Ah, so instead of simplifying each aspect ratio separately, you'd rather expand them both to a common denominator?</p><p>Rendered aspect ratio: 900:185<br>Intrinsic aspect ratio: 900:183</p><p>Yes, that is more useful. In this case, anyway. Would need a bit of code to figure out if normalizing to the lowest common multiple of the width or the height would be simpler.</p><p>Or just:</p><p>Rendered aspect ratio: 4.8648648 : 1<br>Intrinsic aspect ratio: 4.9180328 : 1</p><p>Which is not so elegant, but OK.</p>",
